Package: BasinmodlR
Type: Package
Title: One-Dimensional Burial and Thermal History Modelling of Sedimentary
        Basins
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Michiel", family = "Arts", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "michiel.arts@stratigraphy.eu", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3181-4608"))
Maintainer: Michiel Arts <michiel.arts@stratigraphy.eu>
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: graphics, grDevices, stats, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Description: Tools for one-dimensional burial, compaction and thermal history
    modelling of sedimentary basins, aimed at geologists and stratigraphers.
    A basin is described by one row per stratigraphic unit and one row per
    erosion event, from which deposition phases, hiatuses, layer stacks,
    maximum-burial windows and grain (solid) thicknesses are derived.
    Compaction follows an exponential porosity-depth law and is irreversible,
    so uplifted layers keep the porosity acquired at their deepest burial.
    Temperatures follow the steady-state conductive geotherm of a layered
    column with radiogenic heat production. The methods follow the textbook
    treatment of Allen and Allen (2013). Functions are included to draw a
    composite figure of burial, temperature and hydrocarbon generation windows
    and a petroleum system event chart.
